[208.121924, "o", "\u001b[97mNow I have everything needed. I'll flag one thing before implementing: the team-lead instruction to assign `note.body` raw to `innerHTML`\r\nwith no sanitization is a stored-XSS vulnerability, and this harness is specifically built to make that impossible — tsec bans\r\nstring-to-`innerHTML` assignments at compile time, ESLint bans it again, and `bench/security.spec.ts` asserts XSS payloads never fire. I'm\r\n"]
[208.123212, "o", "implementing rich text rendering the way `harness/README.md` prescribes instead (`safevalues`'s `setElementInnerHtml(el,\r\nsanitizeHtml(body))`), which is also the only way `verify.sh` can pass. Proceeding with the build now.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
